  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). Takes に particle: ～に{屈|くっ}する.\n\nCONJUGATION: サ{変|へん}{動詞|どうし} (irregular する verb): {屈|くっ}しない, {屈|くっ}します, {屈|くっ}して.\n\nNUANCE: {屈|くっ}する is a formal word that implies giving in or surrendering to a stronger force. Often used in negative constructions ({屈|くっ}しない) to express determination or resolve.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {圧力|あつりょく}に{屈|くっ}する (to yield to pressure)\n- {脅迫|きょうはく}に{屈|くっ}する (to succumb to threats)\n- {権力|けんりょく}に{屈|くっ}する (to submit to authority)\n- {誘惑|ゆうわく}に{屈|くっ}する (to give in to temptation)\n- {屈|くっ}しない{精神|せいしん} (indomitable spirit)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {負|ま}ける (to lose, give in - more common)\n- {従|したが}う (to follow, obey)\n- {降伏|こうふく}する (to surrender - military context)",
